@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "How it works";
}

<h1 class="h3 mb-3">How this PoC is put together</h1>
<p>
    The goal is educational: keep the moving parts visible. AI is an extra input channel,
    not a replacement for application architecture.
</p>

<ol class="list-group list-group-numbered mb-4">
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <strong>UI.</strong> MVC views handle forms. The Blazor <code>AiChat</code> component handles conversation.
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <strong>AI repository.</strong> <code>OllamaAiAgentRepository</code> POSTs the prompt to
        <code>http://localhost:11434/api/chat</code> with a system prompt that demands JSON.
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <strong>Parser.</strong> <code>AiCommandParser</code> maps model text to an <code>AiCommand</code>
        (create / update / delete / get / list).
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <strong>Service.</strong> <code>AiCommandService</code> executes that command through
        <code>IVehicleService</code>, the same API the MVC controllers use.
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <strong>Store.</strong> <code>InMemoryVehicleRepository</code> keeps vehicles in process memory so the sample stays offline.
    </li>
</ol>

<h2 class="h5">Example prompts</h2>
<pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">Add a new vehicle with ID 123, Toyota Corolla, 2024.
Update vehicle 123 and change the model to Camry.
Remove vehicle with ID 123.
List all vehicles.</pre>

<p class="mb-0">
    Configure the model name and URL in <code>appsettings.json</code> under the <code>Ollama</code> section.
</p>
